/-
Superfusion / GaugeChi / RouteMatrixProto

**The generator reduction for `gtOfT_mem_interSpace`'s intertwining
hypothesis** (design record: `docs/route-layer-design.md`).

`GaugeChi/TDictGauge.lean`'s `gtOfT_mem_interSpace` turns a matrix element
`T : M_σ(D_{(a+b)+c})` into a member of `gInterSpace K Γ a b c e`, given

1. `hsz : Γ.gaugeSizeR a b c = Γ.gaugeSizeL a b c`,
2. `hT : T ∈ (matrixSuper …).grading e`, and
3. `hT_int`: the intertwining identity
   `routeR'(y) · T = (−1)^{|y|·e} · (T · routeL(y))`
   for **every homogeneous `y`** of the triple tensor
   `(D_a ᵍ⊗ D_b) ᵍ⊗ D_c`.

Hypothesis 3 quantifies over a space of dimension `dim D_a · dim D_b ·
dim D_c` (up to 512 at `realGauge`).  This file removes that quantifier:

> **the solution set of the identity is a subalgebra**, so it is enough to
> check the identity on any set of *algebra generators*.

The sign is what makes this non-obvious, and it is handled by absorbing it
into an algebra map: `signTwist 𝒜 e` is the identity for `e = 0` and the
parity involution `J` (`Super/ParityInvolution.lean`) for `e = 1`, so that
on homogeneous `y` of degree `j`,
`signTwist 𝒜 e y = (−1)^{j·e} • y`.  Then hypothesis 3 is *equivalent* to
the sign-free, homogeneity-free statement

  `∀ y, routeR'(y) · T = T · routeL (signTwist 𝒜 e y)`,

whose solution set `intertwinerSubalgebra` is a genuine `Subalgebra`
(`ΦR`, `ΦL ∘ signTwist` are both algebra maps).  `Algebra.adjoin_le` then
propagates from generators to everything.

Since the triple tensor is generated by the three slot images (an
elementary tensor is a product of slot elements,
`includeLeft_mul_includeRight`), the final consumer lemma
`gtOfT_mem_interSpace_of_slots` asks for the identity only at
`dim D_a + dim D_b + dim D_c` slot vectors — where, moreover, the route
matrices are already given in closed form by `TDictGauge`'s entry lemmas
(`routeL_left_entry`, `routeL_right_entry`, `routeR_aslot_entry`,
`routeR_bslot_entry`, `routeR_cslot_entry` + `routeR'_entry`).

**Contents.**

| § | content | uniform? |
|---|---------|----------|
| 1 | `intertwinerSubalgebra`, `forall_intertwine_of_adjoin_eq_top` | generic |
| 2 | `signTwist`, **`intertwine_graded_of_adjoin`** (the generator reduction) | generic |
| 3 | generation of a graded tensor product; bases generate | generic |
| 4 | `aSlot`/`bSlot`/`cSlot`, `adjoin_slots_eq_top`, **`hT_int_of_slot_generators`**, `gtOfT_mem_interSpace_of_slot_generators` | gauge-generic |
| 5 | `gtOfT_mem_interSpace_of_realRepBasis` — the drop-in at `realGauge` | `realGauge` |
| 6 | the six **slot route entry** lemmas (+ two sign-discharged variants) | gauge-generic |
| 7 | the **coordinate layer**: `realRepBasis_zero`, `matrixFrame_sum_entry`, `realFuse_tmul_entry`, `realFuse_tmul_of_monomial` and its two one-sided forms | `realGauge`, triple-independent |
| 8 | **the triple `(1,1,1)`, end to end**: `hsz111`, `T111`, `hT111`, eight frozen fuse columns, six route agreements, `gtOfT111_mem_gInterSpace`, `gtOfT111_ne_zero`, and **`gParity111 : gParity ℝ realGauge 1 1 1 = 0`** | per-triple |

§§1–7 are the template; §8 is the only part a 512-point rollout re-emits.
-/
